  "generated_text": "1. **Express the volume of the cylinder in terms of $R$ and $H$:**\n   \\[\n   V = \\pi R^2 H\n   \\]\n   Solving for $H$, we get:\n   \\[\n   H = \\frac{V}{\\pi R^2}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Express the total surface area of the cylinder:**\n   The total surface area $A$ of the cylinder includes the areas of the two circular ends and the lateral surface area:\n   \\[\n   A = 2\\pi R^2 + 2\\pi R H\n   \\]\n   Substituting $H = \\frac{V}{\\pi R^2}$ into the equation:\n   \\[\n   A = 2\\pi R^2 + 2\\pi R \\left(\\frac{V}{\\pi R^2}\\right)\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   A = 2\\pi R^2 + \\frac{2V}{R}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Minimize the total surface area:**\n   To minimize $A$, we take the derivative of $A$ with respect to $R$ and set it to zero",
  "grade": {
